# What Cloud Build uploads (gcloud builds submit). The same as the Docker build context (.dockerignore), written out here because gcloud
# reads this file with .gitignore rules: an unanchored name such as "reports" would match every folder of that name at any depth
# (it dropped the Reports pages and the CRM and Sales report modules). Top-level-only entries are therefore anchored with "/".
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.next
**/.next-*
**/node_modules
.pnpm
/out
/dist
/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
/tmp
/temp
**/.cache
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.log
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report
/tests
/reports
/research_notes
/docs
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
**/.terraform
/infrastructure/terraform
/infrastructure/cloudrun/deploy.env
